{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"I’ve been building iOS apps for over a decade, first in Turkey and now in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Germany. The work I care about most is the part users never see: clean"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"architecture, tests you can trust, and release tooling that lets a small team"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ship often. It’s unglamorous. It’s also what makes release day boring, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the goal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Right now that means 70+ public transport apps on one Swift codebase at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"ioki","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", part of a mobility platform that has served nearly 10 million"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passengers. Before that I worked on messaging ("},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"BiP","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 3.5M monthly users),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"banking ("},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"QNB Finansbank","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), live events at "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cisco","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", where we shipped 100+"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"branded apps from one codebase, and public transport at "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Kentkart","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When I led a team at Ecospend, I did the groundwork for each new feature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"myself: the interfaces, the services and the test cases it had to pass. Then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"someone on the team built the rest."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This site is where I keep my CV and write about the tools I use. The pages are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named like a release: the changelog is my work history, the dependencies are my"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stack, and the patch notes are articles."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Currently","level":3,"text":"Currently"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Senior iOS Developer at "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"ioki","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in Frankfurt, working on ticketing,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real-time ride tracking and release tooling."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing about iOS tooling. The latest pieces cover a DocC documentation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pipeline, writing your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" operator, and turning DocC into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a personal site."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Get-in-touch","level":3,"text":"Get in touch"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/in\/haydar-karkin\/","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/releasenotes"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Senior iOS Developer. I build iOS apps that keep working as they grow."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/Experience"],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Work history: what shipped, where and when."}],"title":"Changelog","anchor":"Changelog"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/Skills"],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The languages, frameworks and tools I work with."}],"title":"Dependencies","anchor":"Dependencies"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/Education"],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Education."}],"title":"Build History","anchor":"Build-History"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPipeline","doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/AsyncSequenceOperator","doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPersonalSite"],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Articles about the tools I build with."}],"title":"Patch Notes","anchor":"Patch-Notes"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/ReleaseNotes"],"generated":true,"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations"}],"topicSectionsStyle":"compactGrid","metadata":{"externalID":"ReleaseNotes","title":"Haydar Karkin","roleHeading":"Welcome to","color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"blue"},"modules":[{"name":"Haydar Karkin"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"references":{"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes/DoccPersonalSite":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes\/doccpersonalsite","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPersonalSite","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a personal site actually needs, and how far DocC gets you with each of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those things."}],"title":"Turning DocC into a Personal Site","images":[{"identifier":"card-site.svg","type"